{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ugh, sorry, the screen just dumped me out again. Uh what's going on today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Twisted ankle.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Twisted ankle. Which one? Say that again, I was clicking.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Right.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. When did it happen?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two days ago, at soccer. It's been swollen the whole time.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Yesterday.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yesterday. Mom says two days. Err, so about one to two days, I'll leave it like that. You play soccer?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Chart's up. It says asthma. You still have that?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok. The inhaler dose is blank on my screen. What is it, say it again?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): For the asthma it's albuterall, ninety micrograms, two puffs, mostly before practice.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Two puffs, ninety. Any medicine allergies?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Umm, any fever with this?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Numbness in the toes?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): You ever break this ankle before?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Can you walk on it?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does it hurt when you walk?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. Hold on. With the asthma, are you wheezing?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sometimes. And chest tightness?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok. Swelling on the outside of the right ankle. Back of the malleolus, no bone tenderness. Base of the fifth metatarsal, no. Navicular, no.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): You took four steps, so you are bearing weight. Ottawa rules say no x-ray today.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Vitals from triage are on here, blood pressure one-eighteen over seventy-six, pulse eighty-eight.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think this is a sprain, not a break. Rest it, ice about twenty minutes at a time, and keep it elevated. Sit out soccer till I see you.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's been taking ibuprophen, four hundred milligrams twice a day.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ibuprofen four hundred twice a day? Say that again.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok. I'll see you next Wednesday, that's on the book. Thursday morning the nurse does a peak flow, don't use the inhaler before you come. If the ankle gets worse or you can't walk on it, then we get an x-ray."
 ],
